  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong dark technical art direction, disciplined cyan/green/yellow accents, clear headline hierarchy, and a polished bordered evidence panel. Desktop composition is confident, but the large empty upper-right area weakens balance. Tablet remains coherent. Mobile becomes overly tall and dense: precedent rows lose the desktop/tablet alignment, similarity scores detach beneath badges, tiny mono labels strain readability, and the header exposes only a clipped nav fragment with no clear current-section context. Contrast proof is also incomplete for header links at tablet/mobile.",
    "fix": "Recompose mobile rows into a compact two-column grid with rank and similarity aligned, increase small-label contrast/size, tighten vertical padding, and give the header an intentional mobile navigation treatment with a visible current section. On desktop, use the upper-right space more purposefully or rebalance the hero width.",
